{"game": "deep-rock-galactic", "language": "english", "appid": 548430, "month": "2018-03", "window": 4, "start_date": 1521849600, "end_date": 1522540799, "month_true_total": 896, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-08-29 21:17:59 Pacific Daylight Time", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "41191021", "author": {"steamid": "76561198140541437", "personaname": "Chilli-Göttinger", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/Ave-Dominus-Nox/", "num_games_owned": 218, "num_reviews": 58, "playtime_forever": 94672, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 93963, "last_played": 1772819239, "avatar": "29c14c0534a223d110e2882f5a44e794b5fbcfc2"}, "language": "english", "review": "Its really good. Its kinda cute with that critters, fossils and what else. It has much to become even better as you see the team is really behind it and putting love in this gem of game.\n\nno real critique (just turn of game metrics in the options if you care for such stuff), just suggestions:\n\nreally big caves, even more room-diversity, for challenging long runs would be cool\n\nIt just needs some bugs which punish lonely dwarves (looking at some specific gameseries), besides the leech, so people dont wander off.^^ as the game can be a bit easy with supply pod spamming if you handle waves good\n\nloot bugs are spawning quite frequently, but well, just personal taste. maybe they could spawn more seldom but drop some crafting goods and/or try to run off if you dont kill them fast enough\n\nthe voices are kinda annoying sometimes but thats just a question of taste. after all, they are grumpy space dorfs which in itself is a good catched feeling. just like dwarf fortress, in space, swap booze for dancing.\n\np.s. this is no april fools joke\n\n\nupdate: 1500 hours later in game, it is ...probably even better than at release.", "timestamp_created": 1522536338, "timestamp_updated": 1736645134, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vo